1
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:18,600
I'm going to snatch that
cottage no matter what!

2
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:27,780
This feels good.

3
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:29,480
Ryo-san, a delivery.

4
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,820
Ryo-san, a delivery.

5
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,740
What, it's just Om, isn't it?

6
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,800
Ryo-san, a delivery.

7
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:39,540
What is this?

8
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:43,160
Hey, can you hear me?

9
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,000
It's the Chief's voice.

10
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,220
I hear you. Over.

11
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:54,320
Ryotsu, if you've reflected a little, I'll
treat you to a barbecue for lunch. Over.

12
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,220
No thanks. Over.

13
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,020
Don't be so stubborn.

14
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:03,020
If you want, I can even redo the rock-paper-scissors
to decide who stays over there tonight. Over.

15
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:10,120
No way. If the Chief strips down to nothing,
kneels in front of me and apologizes, I might consider it. Over.

16
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:12,580
What? Don't get too carried away.

17
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:15,880
Ryo-chan, you're being stubborn, aren't you?

18
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:18,360
Even though we finally have a holiday.

19
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,340
Forget it.

20
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:21,600
We'll just enjoy ourselves over here.

21
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,300
Let's forget about him.

22
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,980
Ugh! That Chief!

23
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:29,300
Shall we ambush him?

24
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,260
No, let's take a gamble.

25
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,860
For now, let's secure a place to sleep.

26
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:53,760
Well, there's a convenient hole to dig in.

27
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:58,980
It's somehow cold, isn't it?

28
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,380
What is this place?

29
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:13,300
I wonder if it's some
kind of military factory.

30
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,580
That's...

31
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,540
Gold coins!

32
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,420
Chief Ohara, Chief Ohara.

33
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:07,800
A fax addressed to you
has arrived at the hotel.

34
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:10,260
It's from the station chief.

35
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:13,460
Ohara, I'm sorry to bother
you during your leave.

36
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:17,020
In fact, today counterfeit gold
coins were being sold all across Japan.

37
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:24,480
We managed to arrest the group. From one of the culprits' confessions,
the counterfeiting factory is located where you're headed.

38
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:31,000
We've learned it's on a small island off the coast of Meoto-koi,
the island where Ryo-chan and the others are.

39
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:38,960
Special Mission Agent B-1 Dolphin is scheduled to arrive there at three o'clock.
Join up with him and find the counterfeiting factory.

40
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:42,200
Secure the evidence, the counterfeit coins.

41
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:44,620
Reiko, it's almost time, isn't it.

42
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:48,280
Big dolphin?
I've got a bad feeling about this.

43
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,520
There was also that big
guy in swim trunks, too.

44
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,460
Don't tell me he was riding a dolphin.

45
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:53,480
Could be.

46
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:58,020
The water's shallow here, after all.

47
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,600
I wonder why they'd come here.

48
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,740
Maybe it's a flying boat like ours?

49
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,800
But I can't sense any presence at all.

50
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:08,980
What's that?

51
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:10,680
Grelle!

52
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,580
It's a submarine.

53
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,100
No way, here of all places!

54
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:18,380
Looks like a small one-man vessel.

55
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:19,660
A bad feeling.

56
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:28,480
Loving the sea, protecting justice,

57
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,820
who called him, who called him? Poseidon!

58
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:35,360
Into the chest of drawers he goes,
Tansu-nigon!

59
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,621
I am the captain of the water police squad,

60
00:04:37,671 --> 00:04:39,520
Umidodozaemon!

61
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:45,880
the Dolphin, whose trademark is the
palm tree that never stops chattering,

62
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,640
Chief, what is that?

63
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:51,920
Isn't that even worse than Kaipan Deka?

64
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,680
You know Kaipan Deka?

65
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,480
On land, there's Kaipan Deka.

66
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:57,380
In the sky, there's Gekkō Deka.

67
00:04:57,820 --> 00:05:00,020
And on the sea, there's this Dolphin Deka,

68
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:03,760
one of Japan's top three detectives!

69
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,120
Are you really detectives?

70
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,160
How rude! Just look at this.

71
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,260
My apologies.

72
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:20,120
I'm the phantom detective who only appears on scorching hot days like today,
when crime rises with the heat.

73
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:23,100
Maybe you should just stay a phantom.

74
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:27,200
About this water police
unit you mentioned...

75
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,520
Good question.

76
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:32,020
If it's a unit, it's not just one person.
Besides me, there are five others.

77
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,400
Five of them?

78
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:44,420
I'd rather not imagine it.

79
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,820
Dolphin Squad, deploy!

80
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,560
It's a dolphin!

81
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,520
This is a piece of cake.

82
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:01,600
I used to train dolphins.

83
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,580
I was a glassmaker, then a manga artist,
and then became a detective.

84
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,120
Let's go home, let's go home.

85
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:11,660
I can even do the limbo.

86
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:14,180
999,998

87
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,900
999,999

88
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:19,420
One million

89
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:22,600
There are exactly one million of them!

90
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,580
At 100,000 yen each,

91
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:26,060
times one million,

92
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:29,340
one, ten, a hundred, ten million,
a hundred thousand, a million

93
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,280
that's 100 billion yen.

94
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:38,700
But senpai, what are we going
to do with these gold coins?

95
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:42,260
W-wouldn't that be a crime?

96
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:44,940
It's their fault for leaving them
lying around in a place like this.

97
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,560
But we're police officers, you know.

98
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,780
I'm quitting the police.

99
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:50,600
I'm not quitting.

100
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,300
Then we won't be able to ride
the police motorcycles anymore.

101
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:53,700
That's a shame

102
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:57,920
With this much money, we could go out and
buy a hundred motorbikes just like that.

103
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:05,120
I'll follow you, senior.

104
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,300
Please, it's fine.

105
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,820
We'll buy this whole
island and build a harem!

106
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:34,380
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

107
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:36,600
Looks like this seat is mine,
just like before.

108
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:40,540
Sounds like they're telling us to get out.

109
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:43,540
Cheeky for a chimpanzee!

110
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,040
This pink one is mine.

111
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,580
I'm not leaving!

112
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:51,320
Ow

113
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:54,740
I'm in, I'm in!

114
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:28,200
So there's a counterfeit gold
coin factory on that island, then.

115
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:30,240
Probably.

116
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:32,860
Right, let's seize the gold coins.

117
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:35,660
Could you hold off on that for a moment?

118
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:36,400
Why?

119
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:38,420
The fact is, an idiot who
parted ways with us after a fight

120
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:41,500
No, my subordinate is holed up on that island,
I tell you.

121
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,600
Then leave it to me.

122
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:45,860
That's bad.

123
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:48,700
Hold on, I'll try to talk him down somehow.

124
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:49,920
Please wait until then.

125
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:51,560
What do you think?

126
00:08:56,460 --> 00:08:57,680
Just a moment, please.

127
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:20,400
Ryotsu.

128
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:24,320
Chief, what did you come here for?

129
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:26,160
Ryotsu, I was wrong.

130
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,820
I'll even give you a cottage.

131
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:30,460
I'll do anything, even kneel naked and grovel.
Just come back.

132
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:33,000
Your attitude is quite
different from before.

133
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:35,880
Don't tell me you've caught
wind of the gold coins?

134
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,820
I don't need a cottage anymore.

135
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:41,300
Your naked groveling is disgusting,
so no thanks.

136
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:45,080
Come on, Ryotsu. If you leave that island,
I'll give you ten thousand yen. How about it?

137
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,220
I don't want your pocket change.

138
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,340
It's strange for you to call a hundred
million yen pocket change, senpai.

139
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:53,240
Didn't you already find the gold coins?

140
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:56,100
You definitely found them.
This is going to be a real problem.

141
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:58,540
Ryotsu, about those gold coins...

142
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:01,240
The gold coins! So you did know about them!

143
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,180
I'm not handing over
those gold coins, no way!

144
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:08,260
You went home right away, didn't you!

145
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:11,100
Now you do it too!

146
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:11,800
Yes!

147
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:14,300
Ken-chan, Ken-chan, are you all right?

148
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:15,880
Roger!

149
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:21,280
Hey, let's get ready
for their counterattack.

150
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:21,760
Yes.

151
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,980
What a pathetic bunch.

152
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:33,060
My moment has finally come.

153
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:42,700
Hurry up!

154
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:45,080
We have to protect the
gold coins no matter what.

155
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:48,520
Ryotsu, was it?
This time, I'm your opponent!

156
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:50,140
Yeah, here they come already.

157
00:10:54,140 --> 00:10:55,700
What? There's no one here!

158
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:58,980
That's strange...

159
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,420
Huh?

160
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,260
A submarine!

161
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,360
It's awfully small, isn't it?

162
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,180
Isn't it a plastic model?

163
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:10,980
Are you the one they call Ryotsu?

164
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,240
That's right! Who the hell are you, then?

165
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:18,920
Aaaaaaah!

166
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:22,140
Loving the sea, defending justice,

167
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:25,500
who called, who called? Poseidon!

168
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:28,940
I'll stuff you in a dresser, Tansu Needon!

169
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:31,256
I am the Water Police Squad Captain,

170
00:11:31,306 --> 00:11:33,200
Ubidodo Zaemon!

171
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:36,660
the playful Yashinoki Cut

172
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:39,440
is our trademark, Dolphin!

173
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,420
Your spiel is way too long!

174
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,880
My proud Yashinoki Cut...

175
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:49,760
No good, no good.

176
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:53,020
Nori-koshite, kushite, kakashi-kushite,

177
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,000
Got hit!

178
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,660
I'll never forgive you!

179
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:57,840
Take it!

180
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,780
What, it's just a dolphin!

181
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:06,540
Don't think it's just a dolphin, you know.

182
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:11,280
Splendid!

183
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:12,800
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

184
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,360
No! Not that one!

185
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,640
So what kind of trick
will you show us this time?

186
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:25,700
Main cannon shell!

187
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,240
No way!

188
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:32,980
There's no use running!

189
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,420
Missile!

190
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,700
If they're dolphins, we're chimpanzees!

191
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:45,800
Yay!

192
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,660
Hi-yah!

193
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:55,380
Strange. Why isn't it exploding?

194
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,360
Alright! Go! Keep going!

195
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:00,460
Go!

196
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:01,380
Run away!

197
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:16,200
Whoa!

198
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:17,960
Retreat!

199
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:20,760
Yes!

200
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,800
I'll never hand over the gold coins!

201
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:24,860
How many enemies are there, anyway?

202
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,340
It's just Ryo-chan and Honda,
the two of them?

203
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:28,360
That can't be!

204
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:30,480
I'd say there are fifty,
no, a hundred of them!

205
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:32,380
Surely we're just imagining things...

206
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:33,380
Hey,

207
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:34,840
That's enough!

208
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,800
You lot are getting nowhere!

209
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,940
In that case, let's request backup.

210
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:39,880
Backup?

211
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:02,280
Things have gotten really out of hand,
haven't they?

212
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,720
What's going on? Has something started?

213
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,600
I don't know anything,
I don't know anything!

214
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:13,620
While you keep up the intimidation attack,
I'll land and take control of the island.

215
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:14,480
Very well.

216
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:18,823
Whoa, whether it's Drift or
Dolphin or whatever you call it,

217
00:14:18,873 --> 00:14:20,380
it's nothing special, I tell you.

218
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:22,960
But someone else is going to come attacking again,
isn't there?

219
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:25,640
Hehehe, leave it to me, you hear?

220
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:31,600
Isn't that a US military Harrier!

221
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,880
So now we're up against the military?

222
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:46,340
Let's do it.

223
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:54,580
Alright, not yet!

224
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:56,200
Now, Honda!

225
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,100
We did it!

226
00:15:04,540 --> 00:15:05,820
See you later, then!

227
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:06,440
Right!

228
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,480
Once we seize this, it's ours!

229
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:14,280
Hehe!

230
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:18,620
I've built model kits before,
but how do you pilot this thing?

231
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:20,560
Ugh!

232
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,320
Whoa!

233
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,380
You son of a bitch!

234
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:27,340
Take that!

235
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,160
Whoa!

236
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:32,920
Don't let them get away!

237
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:42,220
Let's see the skills I've honed
at the arcade all this time!

238
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,660
This has turned into a disaster.

239
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,140
Whoa, Chief!

240
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:05,160
What is it?

241
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:11,820
Hehehe, I'm getting the hang of this now.

242
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:14,900
Enemy carrier spotted!

243
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:19,980
Taking down two planes in no time flat,
he's no ordinary man.

244
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:23,060
Captain! The Harrier they
hijacked is diving straight at us!

245
00:16:23,320 --> 00:16:25,260
Ready the Alfox and Sea Sparrow!

246
00:16:27,060 --> 00:16:27,620
Fire!

247
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:58,020
Whoa!

248
00:16:58,060 --> 00:16:59,840
They're really coming at us with full force!

249
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,020
Whoa!

250
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:02,840
Senpai!

251
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:04,860
That's too much...

252
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:06,220
Go! Go! Go! Go!

253
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:06,780
What?

254
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:07,680
Come on, come on, come on...

255
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:10,960
Whoa!

256
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,140
Bazooka!

257
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:13,820
Whoa!

258
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:14,320
Whoa!

259
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:15,260
Whoa!

260
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:20,580
Super-human? Useless!

261
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:21,280
What?

262
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:23,760
Which one is it? The dash device?

263
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:24,820
Which one?

264
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,080
This one!

265
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,940
Alright, let's land.

266
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:44,900
You're holed up on the island,
aren't you, you idiot?

267
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,560
Says the idiot detective!

268
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:48,100
Win-boke Trendaros, you!

269
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:51,860
Don't yank my trademark backpack!

270
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:54,180
Pull it out, pull it out, pull it out!

271
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:17,620
Go on, do it!

272
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:18,480
You're busted, right here!

273
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:29,700
A small moving object is
approaching underwater!

274
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:30,760
Come on, surprise attack!

275
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:33,080
Ungrateful wretches, daring to defy us!

276
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,840
Transform and advance!

277
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:35,640
Surprise attack!

278
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:37,800
You'd resist that much!

279
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:38,660
Then!

280
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,240
Take this!

281
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,100
Are you trying to kill me?

282
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:57,940
Look, never mind that, we have a fire!

283
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:58,340
What?

284
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:00,140
Press that fire extinguisher button!

285
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:01,020
This one?

286
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:04,760
What did you press, you idiot?

287
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:07,100
What do you mean?
I put it out, like you told me to!

288
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:09,700
That's the torpedo button!

289
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:13,680
You idiot,
I haven't even fired one myself yet!

290
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:15,100
Sorry, sorry.

291
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:17,760
We're taking on water!

292
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:21,600
Chief, a high-speed object is approaching.
It's a torpedo!

293
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,360
What?

294
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,340
W-what is this?

295
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:25,160
Perfect...

296
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,400
...hit

297
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:29,540
All hands, evacuate!

298
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:35,140
We went and sank the aircraft carrier!

299
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:38,200
This has turned into a huge disaster,
hasn't it?

300
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:41,020
The US Navy won't stay quiet about this!

301
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:04,860
Senpai

302
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:07,500
I'm going to escape ahead of you.

303
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:19,000
Damn it, it got jammed again!

304
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,080
Senpai

305
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:22,380
Perfect timing, give me a hand!

306
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:25,500
This is no time for that! Look at that!

307
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,740
What the hell is that giant log?

308
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,060
Aaaaaaah!

309
00:20:56,780 --> 00:20:59,620
The island is already
losing its original shape!

310
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:02,360
Even Ryotsu has met his
end on this southern island

311
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,460
Ryo-chan

312
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:06,360
Hey, look over there!

313
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,880
It's Honda-san and the Dolphin Deka!

314
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,740
Amazing! You're all safe!

315
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:11,500
Ryo-chan!

316
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,900
What about Ryo-chan? Ryo-chan's safe too!

317
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,780
Tch, it would've been better for
the world if he'd just disappeared.

318
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:28,100
Delicious.

319
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:31,381
Ryo-chan, the sunken carrier
and the blown-up fighter jets,

320
00:21:31,431 --> 00:21:33,100
they're saying you have to pay for them!

321
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:34,180
What?!

322
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:37,000
You'll also have to pay
for the hotel you destroyed.

323
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,360
I-I don't know anything about it.

324
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:41,520
You're responsible too,
for calling the navy for backup.

325
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:42,340
No way.

326
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:43,920
It's obvious, you know.

327
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,680
Fine, I'll pay, I'll pay.

328
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:48,120
Pay? Where would you get that kind of money?

329
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:50,560
Here's 100 billion yen in gold coins.

330
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:52,480
We'll pay with these.

331
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,460
These gold coins are fake, you idiot.

332
00:21:54,460 --> 00:21:56,640
Come on, don't joke around like that.

333
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,240
It's not a lie, these are the real thing.

334
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:00,060
Compare them and you'll see clearly, yeah.

335
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:03,940
Whoa! Queen Elizabeth has red-eye!

336
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:10,980
Well, there's nothing for it.
Deal with it yourself.

337
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:21,740
I still can't shake off the fatigue.
I slept like a rock last night.

338
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:24,300
This turned into a Dondaian trip, didn't it?

339
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:27,980
When will Ryo-chan and
Honda ever make it back?

340
00:22:27,980 --> 00:22:30,520
Stop it already. My head's killing me.

341
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:41,140
Damn it! Why do we have to do
this shit all the way overseas?

342
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:44,460
Ryo-san, you need to show a bit more motivation,
or we're in trouble.

343
00:22:44,620 --> 00:22:45,880
Look, like that person over there.

344
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:46,840
Dolphy!

345
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:54,660
Next, the big jump!

346
00:22:55,840 --> 00:22:59,300
Hey, Ryo-san,
at this rate we'll never pay off our debts.

347
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:00,460
Alright, alright.

348
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:01,840
Reflection.

349
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:06,820
What the hell am I doing?

350
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:12,600
I hate overseas trips.

351
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:29,560
Lured by the night breeze to
the patio where roses bloom,

352
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:36,160
the moon I gazed up at somehow
looks like that guy's face.

353
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:44,160
They gossip that I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

354
00:23:45,060 --> 00:23:49,980
but I have a mountain of
things I want to do, me.

355
00:23:51,760 --> 00:23:59,060
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

356
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:06,440
I want to be freer than a bird.

357
00:24:07,040 --> 00:24:14,160
A lady's dreams that change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

358
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:14,640
me

359
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:16,920
me

360
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:18,740
me

361
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,540
me

362
00:24:26,820 --> 00:24:28,220
me

363
00:24:31,380 --> 00:24:32,780
me

364
00:24:32,780 --> 00:24:35,380
me

365
00:24:35,380 --> 00:24:36,560
me

366
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:44,080
me

367
00:24:44,080 --> 00:24:44,100
me

368
00:24:44,100 --> 00:24:44,140
me

369
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:59,700
Thank you for watching.

